ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
I wish to thank Dr. Wallace T. Fowler for his initial encourage-ment to enter graduate schooi and for his continued interest and assis-tance throughout my academic career.Also, I especial Iy thank my Ioving wife, Barbara, for her unendirgfaith and support during the writing of this thesis. Between critiqueirgthe rough drafts and typing this final revision, she has probablydevoted as much of her time to this project as I have.Finally, I would Iike to express my deepest appreciation tomy wonderful parents, Jack and Ruth Farris, for their love and guidancethroughout my life and for making it possible for me to attend thisuniversity.
