(or target point) was assumed to be 250 nautical miles above the sur-face of the earth and circular. The total integration time was setto one prior orbital period, or '5631 seconds for thLsorbital altitude.Graphic results of the integration are presented in Figures l.lto 3.8. The orbital plane (X-y plane) is shown in these figures withthe origin of the coordinate system being the target point for rendez-vous. The relative position of the shuttle with respect to the targetpoint is presented for one prior orbital period. Positions of theshuttle after 0, -2000,-4000,and -!5ll seconds are shown on each tra-jectory along with the magnitude and direction of the velocity at theorig in (time = t = 0) . Al so, stable stationkeeping points (on the Xaxis) are denoted.

endstream

endobj
